2026-07-22T11:02:54.397228Z  INFO session_loop{thread_id=019f8937-f74a-7f13-8a67-a1d0cb33b562}:submission_dispatch{otel.name="op.dispatch.user_input" submission.id="019f897d-5ba5-7f61-8ee0-b16c8061df60" codex.op="user_input"}:turn{otel.name="session_task.turn" thread.id=019f8937-f74a-7f13-8a67-a1d0cb33b562 turn.id=019f897d-5ba5-7f61-8ee0-b16c8061df60 model=gpt-5.6-luna codex.turn.reasoning_effort=medium}: codex_core::stream_events_utils: ToolCall: exec const patch = "*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /Users/k1t94/Work/Projects/kaynann/knn-water-vending/specs/001-project-bootstrap/research.md\n@@\n-## Decision: React Native CLI for `apps/mobile`\n+## Decision: Expo development builds for `apps/mobile`\n \n-- **Rationale**: The MVP requires native camera/QR, maps/location, deep links, push, safe storage, and platform-specific permission configuration. CLI keeps native project ownership explicit.\n-- **Alternatives considered**: Expo (officially recommended for many new apps and simpler native setup; rejected for this bootstrap because the project requires explicit native iOS/Android control). Revisit only with explicit scope approval.\n-- **Source**: https://reactnative.dev/docs/environment-setup\n+- **Rationale**: The MVP requires camera/QR, maps/location, deep links, push, secure storage, and platform-specific permission configuration, but it does not currently require a custom machine SDK or custom native module. Expo provides these capabilities while reducing native bootstrap and onboarding cost. Development builds, rather than Expo Go, preserve the ability to use native libraries and custom native configuration.\n+- **Alternatives considered**: Bare React Native CLI (more direct native ownership, but higher bootstrap and maintenance cost without a current custom-native requirement); Expo Go only (rejected because production-like native libraries, push, app links, and native configuration require a custom development build).\n+- **Source**: https://docs.expo.dev/develop/development-builds/introduction/\n+- **Operational choice**: Use Expo prebuild/CNG as the native project generation path. Treat generated `ios/` and `android/` directories as derived unless a deliberate native customization requires committing them. Use EAS for reproducible cloud test builds when credentials are available; keep local build commands documented and usable with Xcode/Android SDK.\n@@\n-## Decision: Vitest for API and mobile JavaScript tests\n+## Decision: Vitest for API and mobile JavaScript tests\n@@\n - **Implementation note**: Select the React Native transformer/preset during dependency bootstrap and record it in the app manifest.\n+\n+## Decision: Expo modules for baseline native capabilities\n+\n+- **Rationale**: Prefer maintained Expo modules for camera/QR, location, notifications, linking, and secure storage in the foundation. This keeps permissions and native configuration explicit in app config and avoids prematurely adding bespoke native code.\n+- **Alternatives considered**: Separate community native packages for every capability (may still be introduced when a concrete MVP requirement needs them); direct FCM/APNs native integration (retain as a later option if provider-specific behavior exceeds the Expo notifications contract).\n+- **Source**: https://docs.expo.dev/develop/development-builds/use-development-builds/\n@@\n-- Mobile native build: React Native CLI with Xcode/Android SDK/JDK prerequisites documented separately from API checks.\n+- Mobile native build: Expo development builds with Xcode/Android SDK/JDK prerequisites documented separately from API checks; EAS cloud builds are optional infrastructure, not a runtime dependency.\n*** Update File: /Users/k1t94/Work/Projects/kaynann/knn-water-vending/specs/001-project-bootstrap/plan.md\n@@\n-**Primary Dependencies**: pnpm 10 workspace; React Native CLI; NestJS; Prisma ORM; Vitest; Docker Compose; PostgreSQL; Redis; Mosquitto MQTT broker\n+**Primary Dependencies**: pnpm 10 workspace; Expo with `expo-dev-client`; NestJS; Prisma ORM; Vitest; Docker Compose; PostgreSQL; Redis; Mosquitto MQTT broker; optional EAS CLI for cloud builds\n@@\n-**Constraints**: No production secrets; no business integrations; no automatic schema synchronization; mobile native builds depend on Xcode/Android SDK/JDK; MQTT contract is intentionally undefined\n+**Constraints**: No production secrets; no business integrations; no automatic schema synchronization; Expo Go is not the production-like test target; local mobile builds depend on Xcode/Android SDK/JDK; EAS cloud builds require Expo credentials; MQTT contract is intentionally undefined\n@@\n └── mobile/\n     ├── src/\n-    ├── android/\n-    ├── ios/\n+    ├── app.config.ts\n+    ├── eas.json\n     └── __tests__/\n@@\n-**Structure Decision**: Keep the two deployable applications under `apps/` with independent package manifests and entry points. Add only a concrete shared tooling/config package if reuse appears during implementation; do not create a generic shared business package. Keep local infrastructure under `infra/`, operational validation in `scripts/`, and the source-of-truth onboarding map under `specs/000-project-onboarding/repo-map.md`.\n+**Structure Decision**: Keep the two deployable applications under `apps/` with independent package manifests and entry points. The mobile application uses Expo development builds and app config; native `ios/` and `android/` projects are generated by prebuild/CNG and are not hand-authored in the foundation unless a later native customization requires that change. Add only a concrete shared tooling/config package if reuse appears during implementation; do not create a generic shared business package. Keep local infrastructure under `infra/`, operational validation in `scripts/`, and the source-of-truth onboarding map under `specs/000-project-onboarding/repo-map.md`.\n*** Update File: /Users/k1t94/Work/Projects/kaynann/knn-water-vending/specs/001-project-bootstrap/quickstart.md\n@@\n - Node.js 24.x LTS.\n - pnpm 10.x enabled through Corepack or the documented equivalent.\n - Docker and Docker Compose.\n-- For mobile native builds: Xcode and CocoaPods on macOS for iOS, or Android Studio, Android SDK, and JDK 17 for Android.\n+- For Expo JavaScript development: an Expo development build installed on a simulator/emulator/device, or Expo Go only for a limited baseline screen check.\n+- For local mobile native builds: Xcode and CocoaPods on macOS for iOS, or Android Studio, Android SDK, and JDK 17 for Android.\n+- For EAS cloud builds: an Expo account and the EAS CLI; this is optional for local API and JavaScript validation.\n@@\n pnpm install --frozen-lockfile\n cp .env.example .env\n pnpm services:up\n pnpm db:migrate\n+pnpm mobile:doctor\n@@\n-## Static Validation\n+## Mobile Development Build\n+\n+```sh\n+pnpm mobile:prebuild\n+pnpm mobile:dev\n+```\n+\n+`mobile:prebuild` generates the native projects from Expo app config when needed. Use `expo-dev-client` development builds for production-like native testing; Expo Go is not sufficient for remote push, app/universal links, or native libraries not bundled into Expo Go.\n+\n+For a cloud development build, when EAS credentials are available:\n+\n+```sh\n+pnpm mobile:build:android:development\n+pnpm mobile:build:ios:simulator\n+```\n+\n+For local native builds, use the documented platform-specific commands after `mobile:prebuild`. A native dependency change requires rebuilding the development client.\n+\n+## Static Validation\n@@\n-pnpm build:mobile\n+pnpm build:mobile:js\n ```\n \n-`build:mobile` requires the platform SDKs. When they are unavailable, run the mobile static checks and report the missing native prerequisite rather than substituting a different command.\n+`build:mobile:js` validates the Expo JavaScript bundle. Native Android/iOS builds require the platform SDKs locally or the optional EAS cloud build path. When native prerequisites are unavailable, run the mobile static checks and report the missing prerequisite rather than substituting a different command.\n*** End Patch";
