ge.json` and `packages/config/tsconfig.base.json`\n+- [ ] T008 Generate and commit the root dependency lockfile at `pnpm-lock.yaml` after all package manifests are defined\n+\n+## Phase 2: Foundational (Blocking Prerequisites)\n+\n+**Purpose**: Establish local infrastructure, validated configuration, migration workflow, and API boundaries required by all stories.\n+\n+**CRITICAL**: No user story work can begin until this phase is complete.\n+\n+- [ ] T009 Create safe environment configuration and ignore rules in `.env.example` and `.gitignore`, excluding real env files, credentials, certificates, native output, dependencies, coverage, caches, and logs\n+- [ ] T010 [P] Create the local PostgreSQL, Redis, and Mosquitto topology with healthchecks in `infra/compose.yaml`\n+- [ ] T011 [P] Add local MQTT emulator configuration without dispensing topics or business payload contracts in `infra/mosquitto/mosquitto.conf`\n+- [ ] T012 Configure validated runtime environment loading and redacted diagnostics in `apps/api/src/config/env.ts`\n+- [ ] T013 Configure Prisma schema and migration commands without automatic synchronization in `apps/api/prisma/schema.prisma` and `apps/api/package.json`\n+- [ ] T014 [P] Create the Prisma service lifecycle wrapper in `apps/api/src/prisma/prisma.service.ts` and module wiring in `apps/api/src/prisma/prisma.module.ts`\n+- [ ] T015 [P] Create API application/module wiring and global validation/error handling in `apps/api/src/app.module.ts` and `apps/api/src/main.ts`\n+- [ ] T016 [P] Configure shared lint, formatting, TypeScript, and Vitest settings in `eslint.config.mjs`, `prettier.config.mjs`, `tsconfig.json`, and `vitest.config.ts`\n+- [ ] T017 Add root orchestration commands for `lint`, `typecheck`, `test`, `build:api`, `build:mobile:js`, `services:up`, `services:down`, `db:migrate`, `mobile:doctor`, `mobile:prebuild`, and `mobile:dev` in `package.json`\n+- [ ] T018 Add Expo development-build scripts and platform prerequisite diagnostics in `apps/mobile/package.json` and `scripts/mobile-doctor.mjs`\n+\n+**Checkpoint**: Workspace dependencies, local services, configuration boundaries, and app-level command foundations are ready.\n+\n+## Phase 3: User Story 1 - Start The Development Environment (Priority: P1) MVP\n+\n+**Goal**: A developer can start local dependencies and the two autonomous applications, then verify API readiness through the documented healthcheck.\n+\n+**Independent Test**: From a clean checkout, run the documented install, environment, service, migration, and start commands; call `GET /health` and confirm HTTP 200 with PostgreSQL, Redis, and MQTT marked `up`.\n+\n+### Tests for User Story 1\n+\n+- [ ] T019 [P] [US1] Add healthcheck contract tests for HTTP 200 success, HTTP 503 dependency failure, and allow-listed response fields in `apps/api/test/health.e2e-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T020 [P] [US1] Add API startup smoke coverage for validated local configuration and redacted dependency failures in `apps/api/test/startup.smoke-spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T021 [P] [US1] Add the mobile baseline bootstrap test for rendering the Expo entry point in `apps/mobile/__tests__/App.test.tsx`\n+\n+### Implementation for User Story 1\n+\n+- [ ] T022 [US1] Implement PostgreSQL, Redis, and MQTT connectivity probes with bounded latency and stable non-secret error codes in `apps/api/src/health/dependency-checks.service.ts`\n+- [ ] T023 [US1] Implement the explicitly shaped `GET /health` response and HTTP 503 failure behavior in `apps/api/src/health/health.controller.ts` and `apps/api/src/health/health.service.ts`\n+- [ ] T024 [US1] Register the health module and configure the API port/startup lifecycle in `apps/api/src/health/health.module.ts` and `apps/api/src/main.ts`\n+- [ ] T025 [US1] Create and apply the initial Prisma migration for bootstrap connectivity only in `apps/api/prisma/migrations/`\n+- [ ] T026 [US1] Implement the Expo baseline screen and development-client entry point without customer journey or business operations in `apps/mobile/src/App.tsx` and `apps/mobile/index.ts`\n+- [ ] T027 [US1] Implement startup verification that starts or validates services, launches the API, polls `GET /health`, redacts failures, and exits non-zero on error in `scripts/verify-startup.mjs`\n+- [ ] T028 [US1] Document local startup and Expo development-build commands in `docs/local-development.md`\n+\n+**Checkpoint**: User Story 1 is independently demonstrable using local services, API healthcheck, and the Expo baseline app.\n+\n+## Phase 4: User Story 2 - Verify Repository Quality (Priority: P1)\n+\n+**Goal**: Root-level lint, typecheck, test, and build commands validate both autonomous applications with actionable failures.\n+\n+**Independent Test**: Run `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm build:api`, and `pnpm build:mobile:js` from the repository root on a clean bootstrap checkout.\n+\n+### Tests for User Story 2\n+\n+- [ ] T029 [P] [US2] Add API Vitest configuration and a meaningful unit smoke test for health status shaping in `apps/api/vitest.config.ts` and `apps/api/src/health/health.service.spec.ts`\n+- [ ] T030 [P] [US2] Add mobile JavaScript test-runner configuration and baseline test execution in `apps/mobile/vitest.config.ts` and `apps/mobile/__tests__/App.test.tsx`\n+\n+### Implementation for User Story 2\n+\n+- [ ] T031 [P] [US2] Configure API lint, typecheck, test, development, and production build scripts in `apps/api/package.json`\n+- [ ] T032 [P] [US2] Configure Expo mobile lint, typecheck, test, JavaScript bundle/build validation, and development scripts in `apps/mobile/package.json`\n+- [ ] T033 [US2] Ensure root scripts orchestrate both packages deterministically and generated outputs are ignored in `package.json` and `.gitignore`\n+- [ ] T034 [US2] Add CI-equivalent local validation documentation and expected failure behavior for missing native prerequisites in `docs/local-development.md`\n+\n+**Checkpoint**: User Stories 1 and 2 both pass independently; API and mobile static/test validation are available from the root.\n+\n+## Phase 5: User Story 3 - Understand And Safely Configure The Repository (Priority: P2)\n+\n+**Goal**: Contributors can discover actual paths, commands, runtime decisions, and safe environment boundaries without exposing secrets.\n+\n+**Independent Test**: Compare the repository map with the implemented tree and root scripts, copy `.env.example`, run a secret scan, and verify that real environment files and generated artifacts are ignored.\n+\n+### Tests for User Story 3\n+\n+- [ ] T035 [P] [US3] Add a configuration safety check for placeholder-only environment values and forbidden secret patterns in `scripts/check-env-example.mjs`\n+- [ ] T036 [P] [US3] Add an ignore-rule/repository-map verification script for required paths and commands in `scripts/check-repo-bootstrap.mjs`\n+\n+### Implementation for User Story 3\n+\n+- [ ] T037 [US3] Update the factual onboarding map with actual application, infrastructure, entry-point, package, and validation paths in `specs/000-project-onboarding/repo-map.md`\n+- [ ] T038 [US3] Document the selected Expo, pnpm, Node.js, Prisma, Vitest, PostgreSQL, Redis, and Mosquitto toolchain and out-of-scope business functions in `docs/local-development.md`\n+- [ ] T039 [US3] Add safe environment-variable descriptions and local defaults without production endpoints or credentials in `.env.example`\n+- [ ] T040 [US3] Verify public healthcheck and startup diagnostics never serialize URLs, credentials, tokens, stack traces, or raw driver errors in `apps/api/src/health/` and `scripts/verify-startup.mjs`\n+\n+**Checkpoint**: User Story 3 is independently auditable from repository documentation, ignore rules, environment templates, and safety checks.\n+\n+## Phase 6: Polish & Cross-Cutting Concerns\n+\n+**Purpose**: Validate the complete bootstrap against the specification and quickstart without adding business functionality.\n+\n+- [ ] T041 [P] Run `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, and `pnpm test` and fix only bootstrap-level failures in the affected application/config files\n+- [ ] T042 [P] Run `pnpm build:api` and `pnpm build:mobile:js`, recording any platform prerequisite limitation in `docs/local-development.md`\n+- [ ] T043 Run `pnpm verify:start` against the local Compose stack and confirm the documented `GET /health` contract in `specs/001-project-bootstrap/contracts/healthcheck.md`\n+- [ ] T044 Run the complete `specs/001-project-bootstrap/quickstart.md` flow and reconcile every command with actual root `package.json` scripts\n+- [ ] T045 Confirm no OTP, authentication, payment, balance, dispensing, referral, or external-provider behavior was added and record residual risks in `specs/001-project-bootstrap/quickstart.md`\n+\n+## Dependencies & Execution Order\n+\n+### Phase Dependencies\n+\n+- **Setup (Phase 1)**: No dependencies; T002-T007 can proceed in parallel, while T008 depends on package manifests.\n+- **Foundational (Phase 2)**: Depends on Phase 1; T010-T016 and T018 can proceed in parallel after the relevant manifests exist, while T017 depends on package scripts.\n+- **User Story 1 (Phase 3)**: Depends on Phase 2; T019-T021 can be prepared in parallel, implementation then proceeds from probes/migrations to healthcheck/startup verification.\n+- **User Story 2 (Phase 4)**: Depends on Phase 2 and can begin in parallel with US1, but final root validation depends on the US1 app entry points.\n+- **User Story 3 (Phase 5)**: Depends on the implemented paths and commands from US1/US2; safety checks can be authored in parallel.\n+- **Polish (Phase 6)**: Depends on all selected user stories being complete.\n+\n+### User Story Dependencies\n+\n+- **US1 (P1)**: Depends on Foundational; no dependency on other user stories.\n+- **US2 (P1)**: Depends on Foundational; uses US1 entry points for end-to-end root validation but remains independently testable through package-level checks.\n+- **US3 (P2)**: Depends on US1 and US2 because `repo-map.md` and documentation must describe factual implementation paths and commands.\n+\n+## Parallel Execution Examples\n+\n+### After Setup\n+\n+```text\n+T002 workspace declaration\n+T003 runtime pins\n+T004 API package scaffold\n+T005 Expo package/config scaffold\n+T006 mobile baseline test scaffold\n+T007 shared tooling package scaffold\n+```\n+\n+### User Story 1\n+\n+```text\n+T019 healthcheck contract tests\n+T020 API startup smoke test\n+T021 mobile bootstrap test\n+```\n+\n+### User Story 2\n+\n+```text\n+T029 API Vitest/unit setup\n+T030 mobile Vitest/bootstrap setup\n+T031 API package scripts\n+T032 Expo package scripts\n+```\n+\n+### User Story 3\n+\n+```text\n+T035 environment safety check\n+T036 repository bootstrap check\n+T039 safe environment template\n+```\n+\n+## Implementation Strategy\n+\n+### MVP First (User Story 1 Only)\n+\n+1. Complete Phase 1: Setup.\n+2. Complete Phase 2: Foundational.\n+3. Complete Phase 3: User Story 1.\n+4. Run the independent startup test and verify `GET /health` with all dependencies healthy.\n+5. Stop before implementing any business functionality.\n+\n+### Incremental Delivery\n+\n+1. Add User Story 2 for deterministic root quality gates.\n+2. Add User Story 3 for factual documentation and configuration safety.\n+3. Complete Polish only after all commands match the quickstart.\n+\n+## Notes\n+\n+- Every task has a sequential ID and exact file path(s).\n+- `[P]` marks tasks that can run in parallel without touching incomplete dependent work.\n+- Story tasks include `[US1]`, `[US2]`, or `[US3]`; setup, foundational, and polish tasks intentionally do not.\n+- Native Expo builds require local platform SDKs or optional EAS; JS/static validation must remain runnable without them.\n*** End Patch";
text(await tools.apply_patch(patch)); thread_id=019f8937-f74a-7f13-8a67-a1d0cb33b562
