2026-07-22T11:14:37.560178Z  INFO session_loop{thread_id=019f8937-f74a-7f13-8a67-a1d0cb33b562}:submission_dispatch{otel.name="op.dispatch.user_input" submission.id="019f8988-13b1-7320-9cac-d09aacba5077" codex.op="user_input"}:turn{otel.name="session_task.turn" thread.id=019f8937-f74a-7f13-8a67-a1d0cb33b562 turn.id=019f8988-13b1-7320-9cac-d09aacba5077 model=gpt-5.6-luna codex.turn.reasoning_effort=medium}: codex_core::stream_events_utils: ToolCall: exec const patch = "*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /Users/k1t94/Work/Projects/kaynann/knn-water-vending/specs/001-project-bootstrap/spec.md\n@@\n-**Independent Test**: From a clean checkout with the supported Node.js LTS and package manager installed, follow the repository instructions, start the local dependencies and applications, and confirm that the API healthcheck succeeds.\n+**Independent Test**: From a clean checkout with the supported Node.js LTS and package manager installed, run the documented root commands, start the local dependencies and both applications, and confirm the API healthcheck succeeds. The API startup check is headless; the Expo startup check requires a simulator, emulator, or device.\n@@\n-2. **Given** the local PostgreSQL, Redis, and MQTT emulator configuration is available, **When** a developer runs the documented local-start commands, **Then** both autonomous applications and the required local services start without requiring real credentials.\n+2. **Given** the local PostgreSQL, Redis, and MQTT emulator configuration is available, **When** a developer runs `pnpm services:up`, `pnpm db:migrate`, `pnpm dev:api`, and `pnpm dev:mobile` from the repository root, **Then** both autonomous applications and the required local services start without requiring real credentials.\n@@\n-- **FR-002**: The repository MUST declare one package manager, a supported Node.js LTS baseline, and exact commands for installation, development start, lint, typecheck, tests, and builds.\n+- **FR-002**: The repository MUST declare one package manager, a supported Node.js LTS baseline, and exact root commands for installation (`pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`), development start (`pnpm dev:api`, `pnpm dev:mobile`, and optional `pnpm dev`), lint (`pnpm lint`), typecheck (`pnpm typecheck`), tests (`pnpm test`), and builds (`pnpm build:api`, `pnpm build:mobile:js`).\n*** Update File: /Users/k1t94/Work/Projects/kaynann/knn-water-vending/specs/001-project-bootstrap/plan.md\n@@\n **Scale/Scope**: Two applications, three local infrastructure dependencies, one healthcheck contract, one safe environment contract, smoke-level tests, and documented root commands\n+\n+### Root Command Contract\n+\n+| Command | Responsibility | Runtime requirement |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` | Install the workspace deterministically | Node.js 24.x, pnpm 10.x |\n+| `pnpm services:up` / `pnpm services:down` | Start/stop PostgreSQL, Redis, and Mosquitto | Docker Compose |\n+| `pnpm db:migrate` | Apply committed Prisma migrations | PostgreSQL available |\n+| `pnpm dev:api` | Start the NestJS API in watch mode | Local `.env`, services for full health |\n+| `pnpm dev:mobile` | Start the Expo development client | Simulator/emulator/device |\n+| `pnpm dev` | Run `dev:api` and `dev:mobile` concurrently | Services plus mobile target |\n+| `pnpm verify:start` | Start/verify services, launch API, and assert `GET /health` | Docker Compose, API port |\n+| `pnpm lint` / `pnpm typecheck` / `pnpm test` | Validate both applications | Node.js 24.x, pnpm 10.x |\n+| `pnpm build:api` / `pnpm build:mobile:js` | Validate API build and Expo JS bundle | Native SDKs are not required for JS bundle validation |\n@@\n-**Structure Decision**: Keep the two deployable applications under `apps/` with independent package manifests and entry points. The mobile application uses Expo development builds and app config; native `ios/` and `android/` projects are generated by prebuild/CNG and are not hand-authored in the foundation unless a later native customization requires that change. Add only a concrete shared tooling/config package if reuse appears during implementation; do not create a generic shared business package. Keep local infrastructure under `infra/`, operational validation in `scripts/`, and the source-of-truth onboarding map under `specs/000-project-onboarding/repo-map.md`.\n+**Structure Decision**: Keep the two deployable applications under `apps/` with independent package manifests and entry points. The mobile application uses Expo development builds and app config; native `ios/` and `android/` projects are generated by prebuild/CNG and are not hand-authored in the foundation unless a later native customization requires that change. Use a concrete `packages/config` package for shared TypeScript/lint/test configuration only; do not create a generic shared business package. Keep local infrastructure under `infra/`, operational validation in `scripts/`, and the source-of-truth onboarding map under `specs/000-project-onboarding/repo-map.md`.\n*** Update File: /Users/k1t94/Work/Projects/kaynann/knn-water-vending/specs/001-project-bootstrap/tasks.md\n@@\n-- [ ] T017 Add root orchestration commands for `lint`, `typecheck`, `test`, `build:api`, `build:mobile:js`, `services:up`, `services:down`, `db:migrate`, `mobile:doctor`, `mobile:prebuild`, and `mobile:dev` in `package.json`\n+- [ ] T017 Add root orchestration commands for `dev`, `dev:api`, `dev:mobile`, `lint`, `typecheck`, `test`, `build:api`, `build:mobile:js`, `services:up`, `services:down`, `db:migrate`, `mobile:doctor`, `mobile:prebuild`, and `mobile:dev` in `package.json`\n@@\n-- [ ] T027 [US1] Implement startup verification that starts or validates services, launches the API, polls `GET /health`, redacts failures, and exits non-zero on error in `scripts/verify-startup.mjs`\n-- [ ] T028 [US1] Document local startup and Expo development-build commands in `docs/local-development.md`\n+- [ ] T027 [US1] Implement headless startup verification that starts or validates services, launches the API via the `dev:api` command path, polls `GET /health`, redacts failures, and exits non-zero on error in `scripts/verify-startup.mjs`\n+- [ ] T028 [US1] Document the exact root startup commands `services:up`, `db:migrate`, `dev:api`, `dev:mobile`, `dev`, and `verify:start`, including the simulator/device prerequisite in `docs/local-development.md`\n*** Update File: /Users/k1t94/Work/Projects/kaynann/knn-water-vending/specs/001-project-bootstrap/quickstart.md\n@@\n pnpm mobile:doctor\n ```\n \n The copied `.env` must contain local placeholders only. No production or external-provider credentials are needed.\n+\n+## Development Start Commands\n+\n+Start the local services and apply migrations first:\n+\n+```sh\n+pnpm services:up\n+pnpm db:migrate\n+```\n+\n+Start the API independently in watch mode:\n+\n+```sh\n+pnpm dev:api\n+```\n+\n+Start the Expo development client independently on a simulator, emulator, or device:\n+\n+```sh\n+pnpm dev:mobile\n+```\n+\n+For convenience, `pnpm dev` runs `dev:api` and `dev:mobile` concurrently. It does not replace `services:up` or `db:migrate`.\n@@\n-pnpm mobile:prebuild\n-pnpm mobile:dev\n+pnpm mobile:prebuild\n+pnpm dev:mobile\n@@\n-Expected result: the script starts or verifies the local service stack, starts the API, calls `GET /health`, confirms HTTP `200` and all dependency statuses `up`, then exits `0`. It exits non-zero with a redacted diagnostic if a dependency or startup step fails.\n+Expected result: the script starts or verifies the local service stack, starts the API through the same path as `pnpm dev:api`, calls `GET /health`, confirms HTTP `200` and all dependency statuses `up`, then exits `0`. It exits non-zero with a redacted diagnostic if a dependency or startup step fails. Mobile startup is verified separately with `pnpm dev:mobile` because it requires a simulator, emulator, or device.\n*** End Patch";
