ice stack, starts the API through the same path as `pnpm dev:api`, calls `GET /health`, confirms HTTP `200`, all dependency statuses `up`, and a total response time under 5 seconds, then exits `0`. It exits non-zero with a redacted diagnostic if a dependency or startup step fails. An unavailable dependency must produce HTTP `503` within the same 5-second limit rather than hanging. Mobile startup is verified separately with `pnpm dev:mobile` because it requires a simulator, emulator, or device.\n*** Update File: /Users/k1t94/Work/Projects/kaynann/knn-water-vending/specs/001-project-bootstrap/contracts/healthcheck.md\n@@\n ## Endpoint\n \n `GET /health`\n+\n+## Response-Time Budget\n+\n+- The endpoint MUST complete within 5 seconds when all dependencies are healthy.\n+- The endpoint MUST return its HTTP `503` failure response within 5 seconds when a required dependency is unavailable or unreachable.\n+- Dependency probes MUST use bounded timeouts and MUST NOT wait indefinitely on a network connection.\n*** End Patch";
